│   ├── protected.js
│   └── public.js
│
├── .env
├── .gitignore
├── package.json
├── package-lock.json
├── server.js
├── supabase.js
├── swagger.json
└── README.md
```

---

# ⚙️ Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the root directory.

```env
SUPABASE_URL=YOUR_SUPABASE_PROJECT_URL
SUPABASE_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
PORT=3000
```

> **Note:** Never commit your `.env` file to GitHub.

---

# 📦 Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/manshi-n/auth-api.git
```

Go to the project directory:

```bash
cd auth-api
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

---

# ▶️ Running the Project

Development Mode

```bash
npm run dev
```

Production Mode

```bash
node server.js
```

The server will start at:

```
http://localhost:3000
```

---

# 📚 API Endpoints

## Authentication

### Sign Up

**POST**

```
/auth/signup
```

Request Body

```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}
```

Returns **201 Created**

---

### Login

**POST**

```
/auth/login
```

Request Body

```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}
```

Returns

```json
{
  "access_token": "...",
  "refresh_token": "..."
}
```

Status **200 OK**

---

### Logout

**POST**

```
/auth/logout
```

Requires Authentication

Status **204 No Content**

---

# Public Route

## Get Public Information

**GET**

```
/public/info
```

Response

```json
{
  "message": "Welcome stranger! This info is public."
}
```

---

# Protected Routes

## User Profile

**GET**

```
/protected/profile
```

Requires Bearer Token

Example Header

```
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
```

Response

```json
{
  "id": "...",
  "email": "...",
  "created_at": "..."
}
```

---

## Dashboard

**GET**

```
/protected/dashboard
```

Requires Bearer Token

Response

```json
{
  "message": "Welcome to your dashboard!",
  "user": "user@example.com"
}
```

---

# 🔒 Authentication

Protected endpoints require a valid JWT Access Token.

Header format:

```
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
```

---

# 📖 Swagger Documentation

Swagger UI is available at:

```
http://localhost:3000/docs
```

Use the **Authorize** button to enter your JWT Access Token and test protected endpoints directly from the browser.

